# SemText npl-flags — preset-flagged runtime config block, six render modes
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house style shared with the other tag prompts).
# npl-flags is a display-only container: its ONE interactive affordance is
# click-to-apply on its npl-flag children (that tag's lane, see npl-flag).
# Its own chrome is a single generated badge, `.npl-flags-preset`, which leads
# the block; its "view modes" are the preset states the schema and the badge
# promise. One example page per mode, one frame.
#
# MODE 1 — element form, preset="production" (canonical):
#   visible: one card; a small accent-tinted pill badge reading
#     "preset:production" (small-caps mono) at the top-left, then the authored
#     flag rows beneath (a monospace name and its value, one row per flag) and
#     a muted note line ("tuning notes…") at the foot.
#   must never: place the badge after the flag rows; make the badge an opaque
#     or inverted block; hide or dim the authored flags or note text.
# MODE 2 — element form, the prefixed source spelling preset="preset:minimal":
#   visible: byte-identical badge treatment to mode 1, reading
#     "preset:minimal" — the source spelling `preset:<name>` is normalized for
#     display, so the two spellings render the same badge shape.
#   must never: render a doubled prefix ("preset:preset:minimal"); shift the
#     badge or rows relative to mode 1.
# MODE 3 — element form, an unknown preset preset="turbo":
#   visible: the same pill badge in the note-warning colour with a DASHED
#     border, reading "preset:turbo — unknown" — the "unknown" suffix is the
#     non-colour cue, so the warning never rides on colour alone.
#   must never: render as an error state (no red, no icon, no thrown look);
#     drop the badge; match mode 1's accent colour exactly.
# MODE 4 — element form, no preset authored:
#   visible: the card with NO badge at all — only the flag rows and the note.
#   must never: render an empty badge pill, a placeholder chip, or a gap where
#     the badge would sit.
# MODE 5 — class-alias container (`<div class="npl-flags" data-preset>`) with
#     element-form flag rows:
#   visible: the same card frame as mode 1, no badge (the badge is
#     element-form component chrome; the class form carries the preset as
#     `data-preset` for CSS/extraction only).
#   must never: show a badge on the class-alias container; render a different
#     card frame from mode 1.
# MODE 6 — JS-off (vocabulary-only, light theme):
#   visible: both container forms as plain light cards — border, subtle
#     surface fill, authored rows and notes as ordinary prose, no badge.
#   must never: show any badge, upgrade chrome, or loading affordance; differ
#     structurally from the dark cards.
#
# Reference snapshots: private-fixture captures of the shipped vocabulary CSS
# in .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flags/ (render-dark.jpg,
# render-light-jsoff.jpg, render-dark-badges-zoom.png). The reference-page
# harness capture is pending (see reports/tag-npl-flags.md). Attachments below
# are live paths.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-flags
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of six reference-page panels in a three-by-two grid
    illustrating one runtime-flags configuration block in its six render
    modes, wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D).
    Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and
    a faint blue radial glow upper-left. Each panel is a dark slate card
    (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, rounded corners, deep soft
    shadow, and a small dim caption bar above it; panels are separated by thin
    slate hairlines.

    Every panel shows the same block anatomy, top to bottom: an optional
    pill-shaped badge at the top-left, then one to two short flag rows (a
    monospace label bar followed by a shorter monospace value bar on the same
    line), one row per flag, then a muted note line. All copy is abstract
    placeholder bars — strictly no letters, digits, or words.

    Top-left panel — MODE 1, preset badge present: a small pill badge with a
    soft blue tint fill and a blue hairline border, containing a short
    small-caps monospace label bar; below it two flag rows; below that one
    muted note bar. Top-middle panel — MODE 2, the same badge pill in exactly
    the same position, size, and blue treatment (the point is that the
    alternative source spelling renders the same badge). Top-right panel —
    MODE 3, the badge pill in a desaturated amber (#FBBF24) with a DASHED
    amber border and a slightly longer label bar (the extra "unknown" suffix),
    same size and position as the others. Bottom-left panel — MODE 4, the
    card with NO badge: the flag rows start at the card's top padding edge
    (no chip, no gap). Bottom-middle panel — MODE 5, the same badge-less card
    as mode 4, at identical padding and row rhythm (an alternative authoring
    spelling). Bottom-right panel — MODE 6, the light theme: the same
    badge-less card on a light near-white page (#FAFAFA panel), dark slate
    text bars, slate hairline border, muted note bar.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, 3D, photorealism, faces, avatars, robot
    mascots, more than six panels, buttons, toggles, switches, sliders,
    progress spinners, error icons, red error styling, an empty or dashed
    placeholder badge in the badge-less panels, a badge placed below the flag
    rows, a doubled preset prefix
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, rounded card corners,
    hairline borders, slate palette with a soft blue badge accent and an amber
    warning accent, six-panel mode comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flags/render-dark.jpg
    role: reference
    description: shipped vocabulary render, dark theme — modes 1 to 5 stacked,
      badge leading each block that has one
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flags/render-light-jsoff.jpg
    role: reference
    description: JS-off light-theme render — both container forms as plain
      cards from the vocabulary CSS alone, no badge
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flags/render-dark-badges-zoom.png
    role: reference
    description: zoom on the three badge states — accent preset badge, prefixed
      source spelling, and the dashed amber invalid badge with its "unknown" cue

requirements:
  subject: six panels of one flag-configuration block — canonical preset badge,
    prefixed source spelling, unknown-preset warning badge, no-preset card,
    class-alias card, and the light-theme JS-off card
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, soft blue
    badge accent, desaturated amber for the invalid badge only
  composition: three-by-two grid, equal panels, identical card padding and row
    rhythm across the badge-less modes, badge always at the top-left of its card
  do:
    - lead each block with its badge when it has one, ahead of every flag row
    - keep the "unknown" cue non-colour (dashed border plus the extra label
      segment) so the warning never rides on colour alone
    - render modes 1 and 2 badges at the same size, position, and colour
    - keep all rows, notes, and badges legible; badges are low-opacity tints
      with high-contrast label bars
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, logos, or watermark
    - a badge below the flag rows, an opaque badge, or a doubled preset prefix
    - an empty badge chip or reserved gap in the no-preset and JS-off panels
    - error styling (red, icons) for the unknown-preset badge — it is a
      warning, not a failure
    - interactive chrome beyond the flag rows themselves (no separate apply
      button, no toggle switch)

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - badge_leads
    - invalid_is_warning
    - no_phantom_badge
  criteria:
    badge_leads:
      weight: 3
      description: Every panel that shows a badge places it at the top-left of
        its card, ahead of the flag rows
      fail_signals:
        - badge rendered below or between flag rows
        - badge detached from its card
        - flag rows overlapping the badge
    dual_form_parity:
      weight: 2
      description: Modes 1 and 2 badges are identical in size, position, and
        colour; mode 5's card matches the other badge-less cards in padding and
        row rhythm
      fail_signals:
        - different badge size or position between modes 1 and 2
        - a doubled preset prefix in the mode 2 badge
        - different card padding in mode 5
    invalid_is_warning:
      weight: 2
      description: Mode 3 reads as a warning — amber, dashed border, longer
        label segment — never as an error
      fail_signals:
        - red or iconographic error treatment
        - mode 3 badge identical to the accent badges
    no_phantom_badge:
      weight: 3
      description: Modes 4, 5 and 6 carry no badge and no gap where one would
        sit
      fail_signals:
        - empty or dashed chip in a badge-less panel
        - reserved blank space above the rows
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 1
      description: Slate Console house palette and hairline borders throughout;
        mode 6 legibly light
      fail_signals:
        - white cards among the dark panels or a dark mode 6 panel
        - saturated neon accents

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-flags
  - media-prompt